Feature: Convert Spark SQL code in fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin.ipynb to equivalent PySpark code with function conversion

  As a data engineer
  I want to convert all Spark SQL logic and referenced functions in the notebook to PySpark DataFrame and function code
  So that all data processing is performed natively in PySpark and remains functionally equivalent

  Background:
    Given the notebook "fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin.ipynb" is available
    And the following modules are referenced in the notebook:
      | Module                       |
      | ../DA_CCG_RSD_EU/Constants   |
      | ../DA_CCG_RSD_EU/ReusableFunctions |
    And the following variables and widgets are set from context:
      | Variable                         | Example Value                      |
      | target_table_path                | "<dbfs path>"                      |
      | partition_key                    | "<partition_column>"               |
      | table_format                     | "delta"                            |
      | compression                      | "snappy"                           |
      | table_name                       | "fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin"  |
      | unity_catalog                    | "finance_prod"                     |
      | environment                      | "prod"                             |
      | project                          | "DA_CCG_RSD_EU"                    |
      | load_type                        | "full"                             |
      | view_unity_catalog_name          | "vw_fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin" |
      | raw_unity_catalog                | "finance_prod_raw"                 |
      | raw_unity_catalog_hist           | "finance_prod_raw_hist"            |
      | config_unity_catalog             | "finance_config"                   |
      | edp_lkp_unity_catalog            | "edp_lkp_prod"                     |
      | dims_unity_catalog               | "dims_prod"                        |
    And the variable 'cl_control_table' is defined in the Constants module
    And the following functions must be converted to PySpark:
      | Function                     |
      | read_control_table           |
      | get_basejob_url              |

  Scenario: Convert Spark SQL queries to PySpark DataFrames with function equivalence (Happy Path)
    Given all referenced modules and notebook cells are available and accessible
    When the conversion process is initiated
    Then all Spark SQL queries must be rewritten using PySpark DataFrame APIs
    And all SQL joins, aggregations, and filters are implemented with equivalent PySpark code
    And all referenced SQL tables, views, and CTEs are loaded as DataFrames using their full Unity Catalog names
    And complex CASE, COALESCE, and conditional logic must use PySpark built-in functions (such as when(), coalesce(), expr(), etc.)
    And all literal "NULL as <col>" must become F.lit(None).cast(dtype) as <col>
    And all date_format, left join, group by, row_number, order by, and windowing logic must be implemented using PySpark functions and Window specs
    And joins between CTEs are performed using DataFrame .join() with appropriate join condition and type
    And the set of columns in the final select/list exactly matches the SQL output (using withColumn or select as needed)
    And any variables, widget usage, or constants are fully parameterized
    And all transformation functions previously imported from "ReusableFunctions" are rewritten in PySpark
    And all special data formatting (e.g., .cast("double"), date_format, etc.) matches the SQL logic in PySpark expression
    And all clauses using "IN (...)" and "NOT IN (...)" are implemented using .isin() and ~.isin() logic in PySpark
    And all data validation is performed in PySpark according to original SQL filter conditions

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven validation of error conditions for missing or incomplete notebook content
    Given the notebook or referenced module <missing_item> is not provided
    When the conversion process is attempted
    Then an error must be raised with the message "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | missing_item                        | error_message                                                                                 |
      | Constants module                    | "Constants module not found. Please provide ../DA_CCG_RSD_EU/Constants."                      |
      | ReusableFunctions module            | "ReusableFunctions module not found. Please provide ../DA_CCG_RSD_EU/ReusableFunctions."      |
      | cl_control_table variable           | "cl_control_table is not defined in Constants module."                                        |
      | read_control_table function         | "read_control_table function not found in ReusableFunctions."                                 |
      | get_basejob_url function            | "get_basejob_url function not found in ReusableFunctions."                                    |
      | Full SQL for P05 and others         | "Incomplete SQL. Please provide full content of fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin.ipynb."       |
      | SQL references undefined variables  | "SQL references undefined variable: <var>. Please define or provide its source."              |

  Scenario Outline: Validate data conversion and transformation logic for key fields
    Given all required modules and notebooks are provided
    And the input data is loaded from source table <input_table>
    When the conversion is executed in PySpark
    Then the resulting DataFrame must conform to the following transformation rules:
      | Column Name             | Rule                                                                                                                                         |
      | invc_entry_period       | Must be derived as date_format(invoiced_on_date, "yyyyMM")                                                                                  |
      | vchr_nbr                | Must be invoice_id cast as string                                                                                                            |
      | invc_txn_amt            | Must be transaction_amount cast as double                                                                                                    |
      | div_cd                  | Must follow CASE/COALESCE/LOOKUP logic as in SQL; fallback to hardcoded mapping where lookup is null                                        |
      | gl_acct_id              | Must concatenate (with "-") COALESCE(gl_balancing_segment, ...), COALESCE(natural_account_segment,...), COALESCE(gl_segment1,...) as string  |
      | actual_payment_dt       | Must be date_format(check_date, "yyyy-MM-dd"); null if check_date is null                                                                   |
      | source_country          | Constant string "NA"                                                                                                                         |

    Examples:
      | input_table                                    |
      | finance_prod_raw.dw_ap_sla_aging_invoice_ca     |
      | finance_prod_raw.dw_ap_sla_expense_dist_cf      |

  Scenario Outline: Validate business rules and error scenarios for data filtering and exclusion
    Given all pre-requisites are met
    And the working DataFrame is constructed from CTE logic
    When applying exclusion filters according to the SQL WHERE clause
    Then the following exclusion and filter logic must be exactly replicated in PySpark:
      | Filter Condition                                                                                                                          | Error message if violated                                    |
      | invoice_accounting_date must be within last 3 years (from current_timestamp)                                                              | "Invoice accounting date out of range: must be >= current year - 3"  |
      | invoice_source_code NOT IN ('Receivables')                                                                                                | "invoice_source_code is Receivables; should be excluded"               |
      | (NOT (invoice_source_code = 'MAINFRAME' AND invoice_description LIKE any of [DS%,DR%,PE%,PR%,PS%,RG%,TR%])) OR invoice_description IS null | "MAINFRAME with blocked invoice_description pattern not excluded"      |
      | natural_account_segment between 4000 and 8999 OR is null                                                                                  | "Invalid natural_account_segment; does not meet allowed range/null"    |
      | cost_center_segment between 9000 and 9999 OR is null                                                                                      | "Invalid cost_center_segment; does not meet allowed range/null"        |
      | concat_segments NOT IN (large hardcoded list of IDs) (both dgccd and dgccd_sla joins)                                                     | "concat_segments contains an excluded value"                           |
      | supplier_number NOT IN ('00032238','00032239','00080463','90000147')                                                                      | "supplier_number is in exclusion list"                                 |

    Examples:
      | violating_row_example                               | violation_condition                                                        |
      | { invoice_accounting_date: '2018-12-31' }           | invoice_accounting_date must be within last 3 years                        |
      | { invoice_source_code: 'Receivables' }              | invoice_source_code NOT IN ('Receivables')                                 |
      | { invoice_source_code: 'MAINFRAME', invoice_description: 'DS123' } | Blocked MAINFRAME description pattern                                     |
      | { natural_account_segment: 3999 }                   | Not between 4000 and 8999 and not null                                     |
      | { cost_center_segment: 800 }                        | Not between 9000 and 9999 and not null                                     |
      | { dgccd.concat_segments: '4009999110011000000000000000' } | Excluded concat_segments value                                             |
      | { supplier_number: '00032238' }                     | supplier_number in exclusion list                                          |

